This policy explains what data this site collects, why, and how it is handled. It covers three areas: the newsletter, site analytics, and comments.

## Newsletter subscriptions

When you subscribe to the newsletter, the following data is stored:

- **Email address** — used to send you new posts and a one-time confirmation link.
- **Communication language** (`en` or `uk`) — the language used for confirmation, welcome, and preference-management messages. It comes from the site version where you entered your address and is separate from the languages of posts you receive.
- **Post-language preferences** — separate enabled/disabled settings for independently authored English and Ukrainian posts. A newly confirmed subscription enables both languages.
- **Short-lived abuse counters** — separate keyed, non-reversible hashes of your IP address and email address are used to limit repeated signups. The original IP and browser User-Agent are not stored in the subscriber record. Counter rows expire after ten minutes.
- **Subscription and consent record** — whether your subscription is pending, confirmed, or fully unsubscribed; when those events occurred; and the consent version and timestamp. A partial language opt-out remains confirmed for the language that is still enabled.

An unconfirmed request retains only the email address, requested communication language, and a
non-reversible confirmation-link fingerprint for up to 48 hours. Expired pending rows and intent
are removed opportunistically and by operational cleanup.

No newsletter data is sold or shared with third parties. Email is sent through a transactional mail provider; that provider receives your email address in order to deliver messages.
Operational Telegram notifications contain only an aggregate event type, language, and preference
action; subscriber addresses and links are not sent to Telegram.

## Unsubscribing

Every recurring email contains a link to a language-preference page. Opening the link does not change anything. On that page, you can immediately stop English posts, stop Ukrainian posts, or stop all posts. You can also use the same signed page to subscribe to both languages again. Submitting the public subscription form again still requires email confirmation and enables both languages only after confirmation.

When all post languages are disabled, a minimal suppression record is retained so the address is not accidentally mailed again. Abuse-detection metadata is removed. You can also send a deletion request to [hello@serhiichernenko.com](mailto:hello@serhiichernenko.com).

## Data deletion requests

To request deletion of data associated with your email address, contact [hello@serhiichernenko.com](mailto:hello@serhiichernenko.com). Requests are handled manually within a reasonable time. Optional metadata will be removed; a minimal suppression and consent record may be retained when necessary to honor your opt-out and document compliance.

## Analytics

This site uses [Cloudflare Web Analytics](https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/). It is cookieless and does not track individuals across sites or sessions. No personal data is collected or stored by the analytics system. Cloudflare receives aggregated, anonymous page-view metrics only.

In addition, aggregate server-side product metrics are recorded for newsletter events (subscription pending, confirmed, language-preference changes, and full unsubscribe) using Cloudflare Analytics Engine. Only the following non-identifying dimensions are recorded: event type, communication language (`en` or `uk`), normalized event status, and referral source label. Email addresses, IP addresses, tokens, browser information, and any other personal data are **never** recorded in these metrics. Data is retained for approximately 3 months.

## Comments (Giscus / GitHub)

Post comments are powered by [Giscus](https://giscus.app), which stores discussions in a GitHub repository using the GitHub Discussions API. Commenting requires a GitHub account. GitHub's own privacy policy governs any data collected through that interaction — see [GitHub's Privacy Statement](https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement).

## Cookies and tracking

This site does not use advertising cookies or cross-site trackers. No third-party advertising networks are present. The only cookies that may be set are functional ones required for the site to operate (e.g. theme preference stored in `localStorage`, not a cookie).

## Contact

Questions about this policy: [hello@serhiichernenko.com](mailto:hello@serhiichernenko.com).
